{"type":"text","timestamp":1788422234141,"sessionID":"ses_f99bb14eaffeLRyeOsPWdJgTt0","part":{"id":"prt_066459f2c001fSf9PWEeNY0Uo6","messageID":"msg_066459c2f001xUTvS6sGIZiicJ","sessionID":"ses_f99bb14eaffeLRyeOsPWdJgTt0","type":"text","text":"\n\nThe `get_value` method has been implemented across all storage implementations with the following changes:\n\n**BaseStorage** (`/testbed/aiogram/fsm/storage/base.py`:52-67): Added `get_value(key, field, default=None)` that retrieves a specific field from storage data without loading the entire dictionary.\n\n**FSMContext** (`/testbed/aiogram/fsm/context.py`:23-31): Added `get_value(key, default=None)` that delegates to the underlying storage with the appropriate storage key.\n\n**SceneWizard** (`/testbed/aiogram/fsm/scene.py`:568-578): Added `get_value(key, default=None)` that delegates to state's get_value method.\n\n**Tests**: Added comprehensive tests in:\n- `tests/test_fsm/test_context.py` - FSMContext tests\n- `tests/test_fsm/test_scene.py` - SceneWizard tests  \n- `tests/test_fsm/storage/test_storages.py` - Storage-level tests\n\nAll implementations maintain data isolation (return copies of values) and accept the same parameter names: `key` for FSMContext/SceneWizard, `field` for storage-level methods, and optional `default` parameter.","time":{"start":1788422233901,"end":1788422234137}}}
